# PLACEHOLDER -- Hemp Bed: a seventeenth bed, in undyed hemp cloth.
#
# The MATRIX is vanilla `entity/bed/white.png` (64x64, the bed's UV sheet) taken verbatim.
# The pillow and the oak frame and legs are left exactly as vanilla draws them, because
# every vanilla coloured bed keeps a white pillow and an oak frame whatever planks made it.
# Only the blanket changes -- the pixels vanilla's own red bed dyes -- and it is retoned
# exactly the way hemp_wool.mctex retones white_wool: the white bed's luminance, scaled over
# white_wool.png's range (212-254), onto hemp_fiber's C4A985 (mid) to E0CBB3 (highlight),
# and continued past the mid end for the blanket's shaded edges.
#
# The linter reads this sheet as an item and raises item findings (outline, light
# direction, pieces). They are accepted: vanilla's white.png raises the same three.

@palette hemp_bed
. = none
1 = 000000
2 = 67502C
3 = 695433
4 = 7E6237
5 = 7C623E
6 = 967441
7 = 9B7742
8 = 9F844D
9 = AA8A5A
a = B38C51
b = AF8F55
c = B8945F
d = BC9862
e = B89A71
f = C29D62
g = C1A580
h = A8B0B1
j = CEB596
k = C2C2C2
m = D6BFA2
n = DCC6AC
p = C7D3D3
q = E1CCB4
r = E0E5E5
s = F8F8F8
t = FFFFFF

@texture entity/bed/hemp 64x64
